The paper’s Step‑0 answer is clear: ordinary set C1P is solvable in linear time by PQ‑trees, while the multiset full-ordering decision problem is NP-complete via Theorem 16/Corollary 17. A naïve “sample a permutation and random intervals” generator would silently fall back into the easy set regime, so I’m now testing the paper’s own Section 4 reduction from a planted Hamiltonian path and checking whether its certificate length and attack resistance can meet the shipping caps.
